WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.339 --> 00:00:06.130
COLIN FREDERICKS: We've talked some
about the meaning of the cards.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.710
But now I want to show you how
they're used for fortune-telling.

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.000
I'm going to shuffle the deck.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.208
And then I'm going to lay
them out in one of the most

00:00:12.208 --> 00:00:14.890
common patterns, the Celtic cross.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.110
Normally, we would be doing a
reading for a specific person.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.554
In this case, I don't have
someone to do a reading for.

00:00:20.554 --> 00:00:22.720
So I'm just going to talk
about what the cards would

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.010
mean in different positions.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.310
The first card is intended
to represent the person who

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.170
is asking the question, the querent.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.510
This card is laid in the
center, upright or reversed,

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.480
however it's drawn from the deck.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.690
And then another card
is played across that.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.200
This card represents the problems
that the person is facing.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.910
In this case, our first card was the
Three of Swords, which you can tell

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.370
is somewhat a bleak card
to begin with, and then

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.710
has been crossed with the Tower.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.600
The Tower, as we've mentioned before--

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.910
it's quite a difficult card.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:13.270
You can see that it's a bit of
chaos, either upright or reversed.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:17.590
To the left of these cards,
we place one that represents

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.320
the past of the person in question.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.500
And to the right, we place a card
that represents their future.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.750
Above, we place a card that represents
the conscious goals of our querent.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.620
Below, we place one that represents
their subconscious goals.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.540
You can see a lot of duality here--

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:42.680
the self and the conflict,
the before and the after,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.560
the conscious and the subconscious.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.160
After that, four cards are stacked from
bottom to top on the right-hand side.

00:01:53.997 --> 00:01:56.830
The first one represents advice
that should be given to the querent.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.740
The second one is about
external influences,

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.547
which could be positive or negative.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.180
Card number 9, second-to-last,
represents the hopes and fears

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.091
of the querent.

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:15.090
This is one card where
it's especially important

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.710
to look at both the regular
meaning and the reversed meaning.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:25.950
Finally, our last card, card
number 10, is about the outcome

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.820
that is likely to occur.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.350
This outcome card can also be
read both reversed and upright.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.890
You can think of it as if you
take the advice, this will happen.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.490
If you don't take the
advice, that will happen.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:44.940
This requires a lot of work between
the fortune teller and the querent.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.940
You need to understand
the meaning of the cards.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.090
But you also need to
understand where that person is

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.040
when they're asking the question.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.130
You can't just do a
reading blank for someone.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.750
You need to know a
little bit about them.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.800
So that's one of the most important
things to know about all of this.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.460
You can't automatically generate this.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:07.850
Just because someone takes the
advice that was prescribed for them

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:11.180
doesn't mean that they are going
to be free with their money

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.160
or that they're going
to be covetous of it.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.310
You need to understand where
that person is in their life

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.670
and what the appropriate advice
to give is based on that card.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.550
You can't just read it straight
and hope that it works.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.040
This is common across a lot
of fortune-telling systems,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.130
including Ifa and the Yoruba tradition.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:33.520
You really need a connection
with a human being.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.710
So this is the Celtic cross.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.960
It's not the only
spread that you'll see.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.650
People will arrange cards in different
ways, especially with different decks.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.890
But it is the most common.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.920
And if you go to a fortune teller,
you might see them use this spread.

